intel-dpcpp (6.2.0-0ubuntu2~ppa3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * d/libsycl-dev.install:
    - Remove redundant openCL header files from opencl-c-headers.
      Keep CL/sycl.hpp for backwards compatibility.
    - Migrate unified runtime loader header files and XPTI header
      files to libclang-dpcpp-6-dev binary package.
    - Change name to sycl-dpcpp-6-dev.install.
    https://github.com/canonical/oneapi-packaging/issues/42
  * d/libsycl-dev.links:
    - move libsycl.so development symlink to compiler-private
      directory to avoid future conflicts where a user may want
      multiple versions of dpclang and libsycl installed at the
      same time.
    - Change name to sycl-dpcpp-6-dev.links.
    https://github.com/canonical/oneapi-packaging/issues/42
  * d/*.{install,manpages,links}, d/rules, d/tests/lto: update
    private compiler path from /usr/lib/dpclang-6/llvm to
    /usr/lib/dpcpp-6/llvm to reflect the DPC++ product name.
  * d/patches/series:
    - apply patch for adding in source versioning to DPC++
    https://github.com/intel/llvm/issues/21509
    - apply patch for adding self-macro versioning to DPC++
    https://github.com/intel/llvm/issues/21510
  * d/patches/dpcpp-0001-add-in-source-versioning.patch: add
    patch for adding in source versioning to DPC++.
    https://github.com/intel/llvm/issues/21509
  * d/patches/dpcpp-0002-add-self-macro-versioning.patch: add
    patch for adding self-macro versioning to DPC++.
    https://github.com/intel/llvm/issues/21510
  * d/sycl-dpcpp-6.pc: add pkgconfig file for libsycl, needed
    for users who want to link with libsycl directly.
  * d/libsycl-dev.{install,links}: add sycl-dpcpp-6.pc pkgconfig
    file to development package so it gets installed in the correct
    location and is available for users who want to link with libsycl
    directly.
    https://github.com/canonical/oneapi-packaging/issues/42
  * d/tests: add pkgconfig tests to verify that the pkgconfig file
    is correctly installed and can be used to compile and link a
    SYCL application with libsycl.
    https://github.com/canonical/oneapi-packaging/issues/42
  * d/control:
    - add dependency between libclang-dpcpp-6-dev and libsycl-dev since
      the clang development package now includes the unified runtime
      loader headers that are needed for compiling SYCL applications.
    - add strict version constraints for all binary packages derived
      from the same intel-dpcpp source package.
    - update binary package name from libsycl-dev to sycl-dpcpp-6-dev
      to reflect its dependency on DPC++ and enable coinstallation of
      different versions of DPC++/SYCL in the future.
    - update binary package name from unified-runtime-adapters to
      unified-runtime-adapters-dpcpp-6 to reflect its dependency on
      DPC++ and enable coinstallation of different versions of
      DPC++/SYCL in the future.
    - remove binary version pinning for libsycl8 dependency since
      libsycl8 may be used by multiple versions of DPC++.
  * d/libsycl8.symbols: update Build-Depends-Package field since
    libsycl-dev is now sycl-dpcpp-6-dev.
  * d/unified-runtime-adapters.install: Change name to
    unified-runtime-adapters-dpcpp-6.install.
    https://github.com/canonical/oneapi-packaging/issues/42


 -- Will French <will.french@canonical.com>  Mon, 23 Mar 2026 14:49:45 -0500

